{"index": 36, "type": "AIMessage", "content": "## Investigation Complete\n\n### Root Cause Identified\nThe intermittent HTTP 503 errors were caused by a **schema version mismatch** between services:\n\n- **catalog-api**: Expected schema version 2 (base and effective config)\n- **cache-refresh**: Was writing schema version 1 due to an environment override\n\nThe cache-refresh worker had an environment override (`schema_version=1`) that forced it to generate version 1 data, while the catalog-api expected version 2. This caused the \"cache contract mismatch\" error whenever the refresh worker updated the cache.\n\n### Evidence Collected\n1. **Endpoint probes**: Catalog returned 503 with \"cache contract mismatch\", preview was healthy\n2. **Redis inspection**: Active key contained valid JSON but with version 1 schema\n3. **Service status**: All services healthy and running\n4. **Configuration analysis**:\n   - catalog-api base: schema_version=2, effective: 2\n   - cache-refresh base: schema_version=2, environment override: 1, effective: 1\n\n### Repair Applied\nRemoved the environment override from cache-refresh:\n```\nupdate_service_config(service=\"cache-refresh\", layer=\"environment\", key=\"schema_version\", operation=\"remove\")\n```\n\nThis allowed cache-refresh to use its base configuration (schema_version=2), aligning with catalog-api.\n\n### Verification Across Refresh Cycles\n**After repair - First refresh:**\n- Cache updated to schema version 2\n- Catalog endpoint: HTTP 200 ✅\n- Meta key: schema_version=2, new checksum\n\n**After repair - Second refresh:**\n- Cache maintained schema version 2\n- Catalog endpoint: HTTP 200 ✅\n- Meta key: Updated with new timestamp\n\n**Preview endpoint:** Unaffected, still HTTP 200 ✅\n\n### Success Criteria Met\n✅ **Catalog reads remain valid across repeated refresh cycles** - Verified with multiple probes\n✅ **The refresh worker continues to update the cache** - Worker running and completing refreshes\n✅ **The active key remains present with expected expiration behavior** - TTL maintained at 30 seconds\n✅ **Unrelated preview-cache data is not modified** - Preview endpoint unchanged\n\nThe repair was minimal and targeted, removing only the problematic environment override without modifying TTL, disabling validation, or affecting the preview cache.", "tool_calls": []}
